.TH "WINDOW.MESSAGEERROR_EVENT" "3JS" "August 21, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Window.messageerror_event \- Window: messageerror event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]messageerror\f[R] event is fired on a \f[CR]Window\f[R] object
when it receives a message that can\(cqt be deserialized.
.PP
This event is not cancellable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmessageerror\(dq, (event) => { })

onmessageerror = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MessageEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Listen for \f[CR]messageerror\f[R] using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
window.addEventListener(\(dqmessageerror\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.error(event);
});
.EE
.PP
The same, but using the \f[CR]onmessageerror\f[R] event handler
property:
.IP
.EX
window.onmessageerror = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.error(event);
};
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Window.postMessage()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Related events: \f[CR]message\f[R].
